WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.953
- Good morning!

00:00:00.953 --> 00:00:01.786
I just woke up.

00:00:01.786 --> 00:00:03.990
It's the day before the big Apple event.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.823
I'm so excited!

00:00:04.823 --> 00:00:06.450
But one of the most difficult things,

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.600
especially for a girl,
is what do you pack?

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.530
I mean, for such a
prestigious, and incredible,

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.500
and exciting event, I really had to put

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.333
some thought into it.

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:15.190
And I didn't want to
leave anything behind,

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.460
just in case I needed it.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:17.760
So I'm gonna bring it all.

00:00:19.099 --> 00:00:20.669
(grunting)

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:22.836
That should be big enough.

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.000
Do you think this is big enough?

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.300
I don't think it is either.
It's like when you go on a trip

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.697
and your friends say, "Hey, pack me

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:30.530
"in your suitcase."

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.443
I'm gonna do that for my friends.

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.150
Not an officially licensed

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.750
Apple product, but, cute!

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:41.320
This is essentially the celebration

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.767
of the 10th anniversary of this original

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.140
iPhone that changed everything.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:46.973
We'll pack him!

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.040
This is the iPod.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.540
This changed music as we know it.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.160
I'll pack it!

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:55.100
I'm sure some of my old
iPhones wouldn't want

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.830
to sit at home. They want to come with me.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.990
I'll pack them!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.200
This was one of my favorite iPods.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.150
I remember doing an
unboxing of this years ago,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.760
sitting on my floor at my old place.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.190
I'll pack it!

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.090
This is one of the red
iPod touches, oh, baby!

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.070
You're coming with us!

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:10.903
Don't worry!

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.930
No iPod or phone left behind.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.820
What am I gonna wear?

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.380
This will look good with my emoji pants.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.630
Let's do a little try-on.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:24.220
Uh, I think I might think about getting

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.330
a different outfit.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.233
I'll pack it!

00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:29.610
(grunting)

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.493
No computer left behind.

00:01:31.493 --> 00:01:33.040
This thing is so heavy.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.420
Anytime I would need to take this

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.120
into the Apple store to get repaired.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.870
or fixed, or upgraded.

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.470
In Los Angeles, there's this place called

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.500
the Third Street Promenade.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.060
If you guys are not familiar with it,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.160
it's basically a big,
long stretch of shops

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.230
on one street.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:47.640
It's all closed off for pedestrians,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.650
so you can't drive up.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.730
So what you have to do is park really far

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.240
away from the Apple store
and carry your items.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.670
And this thing is so heavy!

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.450
I've carried it from the parking garage,

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.970
down many flights of steps, all the way

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.120
to the Apple Store, and then back again.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.180
But we'll pack it!

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.160
Usually, when packing, the best advice is

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.840
to pack the largest things first.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.007
I didn't (grunting)
adhere to my own advice.

00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:12.320
OK, I think I should probably

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.160
rearrange my small items.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.690
So obviously, I'm not
gonna be able to use my

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.903
Mac Pro tower without a monitor.

00:02:23.822 --> 00:02:24.655
That's dusty!

00:02:24.655 --> 00:02:25.488
It's been in storage.

00:02:25.488 --> 00:02:26.807
But what if I make a friend and they say,

00:02:26.807 --> 00:02:28.327
"Justine, do you have an extra computer

00:02:28.327 --> 00:02:29.220
"that I can use?"

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.330
And I'm gonna say, "Yes, I do, friend."

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.430
Squeeze in here.

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.131
I might need another suitcase.

00:02:34.131 --> 00:02:36.330
At least I could put
the keyboard in there.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.790
So I'm basically pulling

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.180
these all out of storage.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.037
If you're saying, "Justine, why don't

00:02:40.037 --> 00:02:41.010
"you sell your things?"

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.620
No, this is my collection.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.453
These are my items.

00:02:43.453 --> 00:02:45.130
This is my pride, my joy.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.340
Most people have children,
I have this and a dog.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.230
What if I need a CD or a DVD?

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:54.450
Well, of course, I can bring this.

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:55.910
Perhaps an iPad.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.490
This is the original MacBook Air.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:02:59.980
Look at this!

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.510
You're coming with me!

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:02.820
So this wasn't the iPad Air, but this was

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.053
the first super thin MacBook.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.160
Yeah, I'll pack you!

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.000
This was my first MacBook
that I ever bought.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.400
This is what I started

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.990
my YouTube channel on, basically.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.210
This thing right here.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.960
We've been through some things together.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:18.793
I'll pack it!

00:03:20.463 --> 00:03:21.653
Oh, I'll pack it!

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.280
What else do I need?

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.000
Maybe a brush because I look like a mess.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.367
I just woke up and I'm like,

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.787
"I gotta pack, for real.

00:03:30.787 --> 00:03:32.940
"I gotta make this video."

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.143
What else should I pack?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.690
What else do I need?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.720
So before the Apple Watch,
was the Apple Watch.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.680
Now this is such an awesome watch.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.350
I don't remember what year this is from.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.300
So unfortunately, the
battery is dead on this.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.890
But when it did work
before, the watch hands

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.810
used to go in the reverse direction

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.270
that normal watch hands would go.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:56.440
Well thank you guys for watching

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:58.340
and thank you so much for all your support

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.173
in the comments.

00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:01.130
I was reading through
all of them yesterday

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.250
when I was reading through my

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.380
little announcement video.

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:04.460
I was so excited!

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.440
I also had filmed that
video a few days ago

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.230
before I'd hit four million subscribers,

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.230
so I didn't get a chance
to actually thank you

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.063
in the video.

00:04:11.063 --> 00:04:12.040
So thank you guys so much!

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:12.873
I can't believe it!

00:04:12.873 --> 00:04:14.690
I've been on YouTube for so freaking long!

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.317
Today I feel like a lot
of you guys were like,

00:04:16.317 --> 00:04:17.150
"Oh, four million.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.310
"You just hit four million now?"

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:19.530
I did, I did.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.363
But you know what?

00:04:20.363 --> 00:04:21.820
I'm still here, I'm still making videos,

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.900
and I still actually really genuinely love

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:24.733
what I'm doing.

00:04:24.733 --> 00:04:27.280
So thank you guys for
letting me entertain you

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:29.740
or letting me let you make fun

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.130
of me all the time.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.250
Which is also fine.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.940
Let's say hi to everybody.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.470
Here, boost up.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.350
This is my sweetie!

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.040
He just went to the groomer's

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.570
and he's looking so nice.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:44.060
I gotta take Manny to his babysitter soon.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.030
I wish I could bring
you to the Apple event.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:48.720
I'm sure I could because
they would love you!

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.460
They would love my angel.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.700
Anyway, thanks again
for four million subs.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.930
Here's to another million or another four,

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.560
I don't even know.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.590
Oh, thank you!

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.240
Are you proud of Mommy?

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.390
Oh, that's a kiss.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.320
That's a wet mouth.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.700
Well I will see you
guys at the Apple event.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.900
Like I said before, make sure you guys

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.733
are following me on Twitter and Instagram

00:05:04.733 --> 00:05:07.180
because I will be
updating there pretty much

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.390
as much as possible.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:11.750
So with that being said,
now that I'm packed,

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:13.420
I have to go put all this stuff back

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:15.480
from where I got it and actually pack

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:16.710
and head to the airport.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:17.580
Manny, I love you.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.413
I love you so much.

00:05:18.413 --> 00:05:19.530
Thanks for sitting here.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.220
Let me tell you what is not flattering.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.603
This outfit!

00:05:22.603 --> 00:05:25.186
(upbeat music)

